  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S.Saroja vs The State Represented By on 28 July, 2022",
    "facts": "This criminal original petition is filed seeking quashment of the proceedings in respect of Na.Ka.No.R2/32154/2017(Charge Sheet No.03/2017) on the file of the first respondent. 2.The case of the prosecution is that the 2nd respondent, who is working as Food Safety Officer, Vickramasingapuram, Tirunelveli District, taken the food sample of Sindhu Chicken 65-Mix Powder from first accused's industries. It was sent for analysis and found that it is misbranded. On the payment of due price, the sample was lifted as per the procedure. Notice was issued to the manufacturer under section 62A of the Act and he received the same. The sample was sent to the food analyst and he sent an analyst report on 09/02/2017 to the designated officer. The copy of the report was sent to A1 and he was also requested to express his willingness to send the sample for further analysis by the central lab. The report shows that it is misbranded. It does not satisfy the requirement of regulation 2.2.25.2(A) of the Act. offences punishable under sections 52, 55, 58 and 51 of the Act. 3.Seeking quashment of the same, this petition came to be filed by the petitioner on the ground that the mandatory requirement of the proper procedure has not been followed. There was a delay in the analysis. 4.Heard both sides.",
    "arguments": "",
